# Workflow: MICRO-UNIT

Spec: MicroUnit
Purpose:
  Define the MICRO-UNIT entity — the smallest parallel-executable unit of
  the SW1 swarm pipeline. A micro-unit is a SUBTASK-sized contract with an
  ADDITIONAL hard budget (D2): it MUST be executable by one subagent in one
  step, with a bounded context pack. Budget-exceeded units are recursively
  subdivided. Every unit is independently dispatchable, mergeable, and
  defect-attributable.

Owns: workflow/micro-unit.sdd

Source: DEC-2026-1011-001 (D1-D3), extends schemas/subtask.sdd

MicroUnit:

  id: MU-<STAGE>-<NN>
      example: MU-BE-03 (third unit of the BE stage)

  parent_stage: <SW1 stage key>
      The owning macro-stage (DB, BE, API, FE, UNIT, E2E, FULL, RF-G, FB, REL).

  goal: <one line>
      Single objective. If the goal needs "and", split into two units.

  Budget (D2 — HARD, enforced before dispatch):
    files:        <= 1            # exactly one file may be modified
    line_diff:    <= 150          # total added+removed+context lines
    token_pack:   <= 8000         # context pack tokens loaded for this unit
    subagent_step: 1              # one Task tool invocation, no recursion
    rule: a unit that exceeds ANY budget is RECURSIVELY SUBDIVIDED —
      never dispatched over-budget. Subdivision re-runs DECOMPOSE with
      finer granularity until the budget holds or the unit is atomic
      (single function / single test / single doc section).

  scope:
    allowed:
      - <paths the unit may touch>
    allowed_actions:
      - code | tests | docs | config | refactor | research
    forbidden:
      - <explicit prohibitions beyond allowed>
    rule: forbidden MUST be explicit; empty forbidden requires
      "forbidden: none (scoped to allowed only)".

  depends_on:
    - MU-<id>
      Units of the SAME stage that must be DONE before this one.
      Cross-stage dependencies live on the stage, not the unit.

  parallelism:
    parallel_ready: true | false
      true when no depends_on and no shared mutable state with another
      PARALLEL_READY unit. Only parallel_ready units are dispatched
      concurrently (P1, P3).
    shared_state: <none | list of locked resources>
      Shared mutable state is FORBIDDEN between parallel units (P3);
      if a resource must be shared it is write-locked and units run
      sequentially.

  channel: R | F
    derivation: channel = F iff parallel_ready == true AND
      shared_state == none, else R (bax dispatch-channels.sdd [DC2]).
    Channel F = free parallelism inside the CURRENT stage only;
    Channel R = dependency-ordered inside the CURRENT stage.
    No channel crosses a stage boundary ([SW1-1], [DC1]).

  agent:
    assigned: <subagent id | none>
    token_used: <int>            # recorded per unit ([I10] extension)
    parent: <agent id | none>    # spawning agent, none for a directly
                                 # dispatched unit
    children: [<sub-agent ids>]  # sub-agents spawned when this unit was
                                 # subdivided
    folder: .specdd/swarm/{run_id}/agents/{agent_id}/
      runtime instance record — context pack + outcome + evidence;
      deleted only after DONE + VERIFIED ([SAL6], [R103])

  self_delegation:
    trigger: an agent that would dispatch a unit exceeding ANY budget
      ([MU-1]) subdivides the unit and spawns sub-agents ITSELF
      ([MU-8]) — depth cap 2 levels below the supervisor ([SW1-9]).

  impact:
    blast_radius: LOW | MEDIUM | HIGH | CRITICAL
    affected: <layers touched>
    review_route: <derived per schemas/subtask.sdd [SB8]>

  lifecycle:
    TODO -> DISPATCHED -> IMPLEMENTING -> MERGED -> VERIFIED -> DONE
    defect path:  -> DEFECTED -> FOCUS -> VERIFIED -> DONE
    rule: DONE requires done_proof; DEFECTED routes the unit into the
      FOCUS loop (see swarm.sdd FocusLoop).

  done_proof:
    artifact: <file(s) produced>
    validation: <test run / review id / scan id; NEVER "looks correct">

Rules:

  [MU-1] Budget is HARD — a unit exceeding ANY of the 4 budgets is
        subdivided, never dispatched over-budget.
  [MU-2] One file, one step, one subagent — no unit may touch more
        than one file or require more than one Task invocation.
  [MU-3] Parallel units MUST NOT share mutable state (P3); shared
        resources are write-locked and serialized.
  [MU-4] Every unit MUST carry a done_proof before DONE (bax
        ../tasks/DONE-PROOF.sdd).
  [MU-5] A defect is attributed to exactly one MU-XXX; the FOCUS loop
        re-dispatches that unit with a narrow context pack (defect +
        unit + BEFORE/CHANGE/AFTER).
  [MU-6] Token usage is recorded per unit ([I10]); stage token_totals
         aggregate unit tokens.
  [MU-7] Every unit carries a channel (R or F) derived as
         channel = F iff parallel_ready && shared_state == none, else R
         (bax dispatch-channels.sdd [DC2]).
  [MU-8] An agent that receives an over-budget or decomposable unit
         subdivides it and spawns sub-agents ITSELF; every sub-unit
         keeps the MU budget (depth cap per [SW1-9]).
  [MU-9] A parent agent NEVER edits a child agent's scope — single
         writer per scope; cross-agent correction happens through a new
         dispatch or the FOCUS loop ([MU-3], [MU-5]).

Templates:
  Instance records live in .specdd/swarm/{run_id}/micro_units/ at
  runtime (never committed, [R103]); creation uses this schema directly.

Navigation:
  SubtaskSchema: @../schemas/subtask.sdd
  MicroUnitSchema: @../schemas/micro-unit.sdd
  SwarmChain: @../chains/swarm.sdd
  DispatchChannels: @dispatch-channels.sdd
  SubAgentLifecycle: @../agent/subagent-lifecycle.sdd
  Supervisor: @../agent/supervisor.sdd
  Handoff: @../agent/handoff.sdd
  LoopProtection: @../tasks/LOOP-PROTECTION.sdd
  ExecutionLoop: @../workflow/execution-loop.sdd

State: +
  (Phase 160 — created as the parallel-executable unit contract for
   /sdd-swarm; a sized, single-step, single-file instance of the
   SUBTASK discipline with a hard token/file/line budget per DEC-2026-1011-001 D2)
  (Phase 161 — extended per DEC-2026-1011-002 D2/D3: channel R|F
   derivation, self-delegation, agent lineage (parent/children) and
   runtime folder fields, [MU-7]-[MU-9])